Command: ['/tmp/ov-1254-target/debug/farcooler', 'workflow', 'resolve', '--help']
Settle a run whose worktree step is Uncertain because its git never finished, or a cancel waiting on one. The runner looks first: with nothing of the tree there (no directory, no worktree git lists, no branch it would have made), the step fails and can be retried; anything there is named, to take away by hand first

Usage: farcooler workflow resolve [OPTIONS] --run <RUN> --pin <PIN> --command-id <COMMAND_ID> --revision <REVISION> --epoch <EPOCH> --sequence <SEQUENCE> <WORKSPACE> <ITEM>

Arguments:
  <WORKSPACE>
          

  <ITEM>
          

Options:
      --json
          Emit machine-readable JSON. The Mac app consumes this rather than scraping human output

      --run <RUN>
          

      --pin <PIN>
          

      --runner <TARGET>
          Operate on another runner, as `user@host` or an ssh config alias.
          
          Runs the same protocol over ssh, so this flag reaches a runner exactly as your own ssh does: one ssh can't reach, this can't either. A runner's tunnel is the apps' route into it, and is not what this flag uses.

      --command-id <COMMAND_ID>
          Keep this identity and every argument unchanged when retrying a lost reply

      --revision <REVISION>
          

      --epoch <EPOCH>
          

      --sequence <SEQUENCE>
          

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

